Content:
## Dialog Form Pattern (Authoritative — All Dialog Forms MUST Follow This)

This pattern is established by the `OllamaConnectionForm` / `OllamaSettings` components in Cyrena.Runtime.Ollama and is the **only** correct way to implement dialog forms in this solution.

---

### 1. The Dialog Form Component (e.g. `OllamaConnectionForm.razor`)

**Razor file structure:**
- Wraps content in `<MudDialog>` — **NOT** `<MudDialog @bind-Visible="...">`
- Uses `<DialogContent>` and `<DialogActions>` named render fragments
- Contains a `<MudForm @ref="_form" Model="Model">` for validation
- Action buttons call methods on the code-behind, which close the dialog via the cascading `IMudDialogInstance`

```razor
<MudDialog>
    <DialogContent>
        <MudForm @ref="_form" Model="Model">
            <MudTextField @bind-Value="Model.SomeProperty" Label="Some Property" Required="true" />
            <!-- other fields -->
        </MudForm>
    </DialogContent>
    <DialogActions>
        <MudButton OnClick="Cancel" Color="Color.Error">Cancel</MudButton>
        <MudButton OnClick="Submit">Submit</MudButton>
    </DialogActions>
</MudDialog>
```

**Code-behind (`*.razor.cs`):**
- `[CascadingParameter] private IMudDialogInstance MudDialog { get; set; } = default!;` — **required**
- `[Parameter] public MyModel Model { get; set; } = default!;` — the model to edit/create
- `Submit()` validates the form, then closes with `DialogResult.Ok(Model)`
- `Cancel()` closes with `DialogResult.Cancel()`

```csharp
public partial class MyDialogForm
{
    [Parameter] 
    public MyModel Model { get; set; } = default!;

    [CascadingParameter]
    private IMudDialogInstance MudDialog { get; set; } = default!;

    private MudForm _form = default!;

    private async Task Submit()
    {       
        await _form.ValidateAsync();
        if (_form.IsValid)
            MudDialog.Close(DialogResult.Ok(Model));
    }

    private void Cancel()
    {
        MudDialog.Close(DialogResult.Cancel());
    }
}
```

**Critical rules for the dialog form component:**
- **NO** `@bind-Visible` or `@bind-IsVisible` on `<MudDialog>` — the dialog is shown via `IDialogService`, not local state
- **NO** `TitleContent` render fragment — the title is passed as the first argument to `IDialogService.ShowAsync()`
- **MUST** use `[CascadingParameter] IMudDialogInstance` to get the dialog instance
- **MUST** call `MudDialog.Close(DialogResult.Ok(...))` or `DialogResult.Cancel()` to close
- **MUST** use `<MudForm>` with `@ref` for validation before closing

---

### 2. The Caller Component (e.g. `OllamaSettings.razor.cs`)

**Inject `IDialogService`:**
```csharp
[Inject] private IDialogService _dialog { get; set; } = default!;
```

**Show the dialog:**
```csharp
var parameters = new DialogParameters<MyDialogForm>
{
    { x => x.Model, model }
};
var options = new DialogOptions { CloseOnEscapeKey = true, MaxWidth = MaxWidth.Small, FullWidth = true };
var dialog = await _dialog.ShowAsync<MyDialogForm>("Dialog Title", parameters, options);
var result = await dialog.Result;
```

**Check result and act:**
```csharp
if (result is { Canceled: false })
{
    // User clicked Submit — model has been modified
    await _store.UpdateAsync(model);
    // refresh UI
}
```

**For confirmation dialogs (delete, etc.):**
```csharp
var parameters = new DialogParameters<MudMessageBox>
{
    { x => x.Title, "Delete Item" },
    { x => x.Message, $"Are you sure you want to delete {item.Name}?" },
    { x => x.YesText, "Delete" },
    { x => x.CancelText, "Cancel" }
};
var dialog = await _dialog.ShowAsync<MudMessageBox>("", parameters);
var result = await dialog.Result;
if (result is { Canceled: false })
{
    // confirmed
}
```

**Critical rules for the caller:**
- **ALWAYS** use `DialogParameters<T>` with typed lambda expressions `{ x => x.Property, value }`
- **ALWAYS** await `dialog.Result` to get the `DialogResult`
- **ALWAYS** check `result.Canceled` before acting on the result
- **NEVER** use `DialogResult.Ok<bool>(true)` or boolean return values — pass the model itself via `DialogResult.Ok(Model)`
- **NEVER** use `await result.GetReturnValueAsync<bool>()` — check `result.Canceled` and use the model directly

---

### 3. What NOT to do (Anti-patterns)

| Anti-pattern | Why it's wrong |
|-------------|----------------|
| `<MudDialog @bind-Visible="_show">` | This is for inline dialogs, not `IDialogService` dialogs |
| `<MudDialog @bind-IsVisible="_show">` | Same — wrong API for service-based dialogs |
| `DialogResult.Ok(true)` / `Ok(false)` | Don't return booleans — return the actual model |
| `await result.GetReturnValueAsync<bool>()` | Don't extract booleans — check `result.Canceled` |
| `new DialogParameters { { "Model", model } }` | Use typed `DialogParameters<T>` with lambdas |
| `new DialogParameters { { nameof(MyDialog.Model), model } }` | Use typed `DialogParameters<T>` with lambdas |
| Passing title via `<TitleContent>` in the dialog form | Title goes in `ShowAsync()` first argument |
| Using `DialogService` (BootstrapBlazor) or `ResultDialogOption` | These are old APIs, not MudBlazor |

---

### 4. Summary of the Pattern

```
Caller Component                          Dialog Form Component
----------------                          ---------------------

1. Creates model                          1. Receives model via [Parameter]
2. Builds DialogParameters<T>             2. Wraps in <MudDialog> (no @bind-Visible)
3. Calls _dialog.ShowAsync<T>(title, ...) 3. Uses <DialogContent> + <DialogActions>
4. Awaits dialog.Result                   4. Validates <MudForm> on Submit
5. Checks result.Canceled                 5. Calls MudDialog.Close(DialogResult.Ok(Model))
6. Acts on result                         6. Or MudDialog.Close(DialogResult.Cancel())
```

This is the **only** correct dialog form pattern for this solution. Any new dialog form must follow this exactly.
